WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.269
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:15.472
Unit fifteen: Stories and Legends. In this unit, you will tell a story using the past continuous.

4
00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.357
Legend.

5
00:00:18.057 --> 00:00:21.136
Legend means an old story that may or may not be true.

6
00:00:21.436 --> 00:00:23.737
There is a legend about Preah Thong and Neang Neak.

7
00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:27.113
Your turn. Say: Legend.

8
00:00:29.813 --> 00:00:30.686
Legend.

9
00:00:31.683 --> 00:00:32.487
Story.

10
00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:36.731
Story means a description of events, real or imagined.

11
00:00:37.031 --> 00:00:39.576
Grandpa tells us a story every night.

12
00:00:40.276 --> 00:00:42.801
Your turn. Say: Story.

13
00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:46.432
Story.

14
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:48.139
Hero.

15
00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:51.233
Hero means a brave person in a story.

16
00:00:51.533 --> 00:00:53.219
The hero saved the village.

17
00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:56.653
Your turn. Say: Hero.

18
00:00:59.353 --> 00:01:00.134
Hero.

19
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.012
Magic.

20
00:01:02.712 --> 00:01:06.441
Magic means a special power that makes impossible things happen.

21
00:01:06.741 --> 00:01:08.590
The princess had magic powers.

22
00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.919
Your turn. Say: Magic.

23
00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:15.550
Magic.

24
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.004
Once upon a time.

25
00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:22.155
Once upon a time means words that begin a traditional story.

26
00:01:22.455 --> 00:01:24.733
Once upon a time, there was a clever rabbit.

27
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:28.074
Your turn. Say: Once upon a time.

28
00:01:30.774 --> 00:01:32.018
Once upon a time.

29
00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:33.797
Moral.

30
00:01:34.497 --> 00:01:37.600
Moral means the lesson a story teaches.

31
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.015
The moral is: be honest.

32
00:01:40.715 --> 00:01:43.054
Your turn. Say: Moral.

33
00:01:45.754 --> 00:01:46.593
Moral.

34
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:48.236
Tell.

35
00:01:48.936 --> 00:01:51.690
Tell means to say a story or information to someone.

36
00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:53.375
Can you tell me a legend?

37
00:01:54.075 --> 00:01:56.390
Your turn. Say: Tell.

38
00:01:59.090 --> 00:01:59.882
Tell.

39
00:02:00.883 --> 00:02:02.082
Grandparents.

40
00:02:02.782 --> 00:02:05.513
Grandparents means the parents of your mother or father.

41
00:02:05.813 --> 00:02:08.195
My grandparents know many old stories.

42
00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:11.873
Your turn. Say: Grandparents.

43
00:02:14.573 --> 00:02:15.690
Grandparents.

44
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:18.706
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:19.006 --> 00:02:22.016
Sreypich, do you know the story of the clever rabbit?

46
00:02:23.317 --> 00:02:25.934
Yes! The rabbit was walking near a river.

47
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.367
What happened next?

48
00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:32.356
While he was drinking water, a crocodile came!

49
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:34.941
What was the moral?

50
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:39.878
Use your brain, not your size. My grandma told me.

51
00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:44.611
Grammar focus: Past continuous (was walking).

52
00:02:44.911 --> 00:02:47.572
The rabbit was walking when he saw a crocodile.

53
00:02:47.872 --> 00:02:52.905
Use the past continuous for a longer action in the past. A short action can interrupt it.

54
00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:56.383
Now read and listen. The Clever Rabbit.

55
00:02:56.683 --> 00:03:00.389
Once upon a time, a little rabbit was walking near a river.

56
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:04.078
He was looking for sweet fruit on the other side.

57
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:08.706
While he was thinking, a big crocodile swam past.

58
00:03:10.017 --> 00:03:13.328
The rabbit tricked the crocodile and crossed the river on its back.

59
00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:18.532
The moral of the story is: a clever mind is stronger than big teeth.

60
00:03:19.817 --> 00:03:22.376
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:22.676 --> 00:03:24.676
The rabbit blank walking near the river.

62
00:03:24.976 --> 00:03:28.025
A, was. B, were. C, is.

63
00:03:32.017 --> 00:03:33.947
The answer is A: was.

64
00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.902
The lesson a story teaches is the blank.

65
00:03:38.202 --> 00:03:42.529
A, moral. B, legend. C, hero.

66
00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:48.249
The answer is A: moral.

67
00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.168
A brave person in a story is a blank.

68
00:03:52.468 --> 00:03:55.517
A, hero. B, king. C, moral.

69
00:03:59.517 --> 00:04:01.888
The answer is A: hero.

70
00:04:03.383 --> 00:04:06.721
Now it's your turn to speak. Tell a story or legend you know.

71
00:04:12.021 --> 00:04:18.818
Once upon a time, a rabbit was walking near a river. While he was drinking, a crocodile came, but the clever rabbit tricked him.

72
00:04:19.118 --> 00:04:21.117
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:22.117 --> 00:04:26.232
Great work today! You learned eight new words and past continuous (was walking).

74
00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:30.612
Today's value is tradition. Learn and keep our special traditions.

75
00:04:30.912 --> 00:04:33.623
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:33.923 --> 00:04:36.320
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

